Ran 62 tests across 3 files. [44.49s]
[exit 0]
```

What the two stub-upstream runs prove:

- **GitLab path.** The connection's base URL is `https://gitlab.test`; the clone's info/refs and
  upload-pack requests arrive at `https://gitlab.test/acme/app.git/...` with HTTP Basic
  (`oauth2:<token>`), and no request carries our `agtgit1` credential. The push asks
  `https://gitlab.test/api/v4/projects/acme%2Fapp/repository/merge_base?refs[]=<old>&refs[]=<parent>`
  with `PRIVATE-TOKEN: <token>`; when the merge base is the old tip, receive-pack goes to the instance,
  and when it is not, nothing reaches receive-pack.
- **GitHub path.** The GitHub tests still send `https://github.test/acme/app.git/info/refs` and
  `git-upload-pack` (the fake upstream's URL, the production constant is unchanged), with
  `Basic base64("x-access-token:<GitHub token>")`, and a push still asks
  `/repos/acme/app/compare/<old>...<oid>` with `Bearer`. `git.test.ts` asserts the exact call list and
  header; no `private-token` header is sent on the GitHub path.

